<title>GREECE: PARLIAMENT TO CONSIDER PROPOSAL FOR BOURSE PROBE.</title>
<headline>PARLIAMENT TO CONSIDER PROPOSAL FOR BOURSE PROBE.</headline>
<dateline>ATHENS 1997-01-13</dateline>
<text>
<p>Greece's parliament will discuss on Monday a proposal by about 70 political opposition deputies to set up a parliamentary investigating committee to probe into the recent Delta Securities scandal at the Athens bourse.</p>
<p>Parliament sources said the government will oppose the proposal on grounds that such an investigation would damage market sentiment at the exchange.</p>
<p>Delta Securities which defaulted on payment of 2.6 billion drachmas with the bourse's clearing house caused an uproar which closed down the bourse for four days in November last year. --George Georgiopoulos, Athens Newsroom +301 3311812-4</p>
</text>
